<http://data.silknow.org/object/d5b02bc7-bce7-3395-b09d-e7b3d9fecc95>
        a                              ecrm:E22_Man-Made_Object ;
        rdfs:comment                   "Woman's petticoat 1750-70, British; White silk satin, quilted with leaves, flowers, zig-zags"@en , "Woman’s petticoat of white silk satin, lined with undyed glazed worsted and wadded with a thin layer of wool.  It is quilted in running stitch with white silk thread in horizontal rows of leaves, flowers, ogee arches, zig-zags and undulating lines.  The petticoat is made of six panels of silk with pocket openings in the side seams bound with white satin.  There is a wide box pleat at centre front with pleats on each side and pleats either side of the centre back opening.  The waist is bound with 1-inch (2.5 cm) wide linen tape, which forms the ties.  The hem is bound with 1-inch (2.5 cm) wide beige silk ribbon."@en ;
        ecrm:P138i_has_representation  <http://data.silknow.org/image/939c5772-71ba-3306-86a3-165a5df63ad5> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note               "Woman's petticoat 1750-70, British; White silk satin, quilted with leaves, flowers, zig-zags"@en , "Woman’s petticoat of white silk satin, lined with undyed glazed worsted and wadded with a thin layer of wool.  It is quilted in running stitch with white silk thread in horizontal rows of leaves, flowers, ogee arches, zig-zags and undulating lines.  The petticoat is made of six panels of silk with pocket openings in the side seams bound with white satin.  There is a wide box pleat at centre front with pleats on each side and pleats either side of the centre back opening.  The waist is bound with 1-inch (2.5 cm) wide linen tape, which forms the ties.  The hem is bound with 1-inch (2.5 cm) wide beige silk ribbon."@en ;
